Add alternate write_ecmascript() API to Zmij

The differences between Zmij's shortest-representation output format and
the format required by ECMAScript are: (1) single-digit exponents must
be output without a leading 0, so "e-7" instead of "e-07"; (2) fixed
notation is used for exponents -6 through +20; (3) -0 and -NaN are
output without a sign; (4) the spelling of "NaN" and "Infinity" are
changed.

This patch implements all of these differences in a new API,
zmij::write_ecmascript(). In order to keep the diff as small and
manageable as possible for rebases, it reuses the library's existing
code paths as much as possible, templatizing zmij::detail::write() plus
a few other things on an "ecmascript" boolean so that we can implement
the changes inside an "if constexpr (ecmascript)" block.

The alternative is a shorter patch (or series of shorter patches) that
is trickier to rebase, and which results in an inconsistent state in the
library; for example, things like the f32 code and write_constexpr()
aren't used by SpiderMonkey, and they would behave differently than the
f64 code.

The fixed-notation parts deserve some extra explanation. Unfortunately
it isn't quite as simple as changing min_fixed_dec_exp and
max_fixed_dec_exp, as there are other places where the assumption of no
more than 16 digits is baked in:

* We need to write extra trailing zeros for 17 digits or more. 

* We need an ecmascript_buffer_size separate from double_buffer_size to
  accommodate more scratch space for a memmove(). (The alternative would
  be to cap the memmove, but I noticed that the current buffer size is
  already much larger than the maximum output string size, in order to
  accommodate this memmove in the 16-digit case.)

* There's one SSE4-only path that needs an adjustment; the SSE4 code
  would unconditionally write the last digit at position 16 in case the
  decimal point was inside the vector; if it wasn't, pos 16 would either
  be overwritten or past the end of the output. The latter assumption no
  longer holds, because with max_fixed_dec_exp > 16 there may be digits
  following.
